'''''Agrostis castellana''''', the '''highland bent''', '''dryland bent''' or '''dryland browntop''', is a species of [[Pooideae|cool-season grass]] in the family [[Poaceae]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://identify.plantnet.org/the-plant-list/species/Agrostis%20castellana%20Boiss.%20&%20Reut./data |title=''Agrostis castellana'' Boiss. & Reut. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2022 |website=plantnet.org |publisher=Pl@ntNet |access-date=28 January 2022 |quote=... Highland Bentgrass }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ukwildflowers.com/Web_pages/agrostis_castellana_highland_bent.htm |title=''Agrostis castellana'' Highland Bent I |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=29 January 2013 |website=ukwildflowers.com |publisher=British Wild Flower |access-date=28 January 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://swbiodiversity.org/seinet/taxa/index.php?taxon=71249 |title=''Agrostis castellana'' Boiss. & Reuter |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=swbiodiversity.org |publisher=SEINet Portal Network |access-date=28 January 2022 }}</ref> It is native to [[Macaronesian Biogeographic Region|Macaronesia]] and the [[Mediterranean Basin|Mediterranean]], has been widely introduced elsewhere, and is considered an [[invasive species]] in some locales.<ref name="271894-2" >{{cite POWO |id=271894-2 |title=''Agrostis castellana'' Boiss. & Reut. |access-date=28 January 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cabi.org/isc/datasheet/112062 |title=''Agrostis castellana'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=19 November 2019 |website=Invasive Species Compendium |publisher=CAB International |access-date=28 January 2022 }}</ref> It is a [[hyperaccumulator]] of zinc and lead.<ref name="1_of_1880_Google_Scholar_results" >{{cite book |chapter=Heavy Metals in Native Mediterranean Grassland Species Growing at Abandoned Mine Sites: Ecotoxicological Assessment and Phytoremediation of Polluted Soils |title=Heavy Metal Contamination of Soils |series=Soil Biology |year=2015 |last1=Gutiérrez-Ginés |first1=Mª J. |last2=Pastor |first2=J. |last3=Hernández |first3=A. J. |volume=44 |pages=159–178 |doi=10.1007/978-3-319-14526-6_9 |isbn=978-3-319-14525-9 }}</ref><ref name="2_of_1880_Google_Scholar_results" >{{cite journal |title=The role of phytochelatins in constitutive and adaptive heavy metal tolerances in hyperaccumulator and non-hyperaccumulator metallophytes |year=2002 |last1=Schat |first1=H. |last2=Llugany |first2=M. |last3=Vooijs |first3=R. |last4=Hartley-Whitaker |first4=J. |last5=Bleeker |first5=P. M. |journal=Journal of Experimental Botany |volume=53 |issue=379 |pages=2381–2392 |doi=10.1093/jxb/erf107 |pmid=12432030 |doi-access=free |hdl=1871/29488 |hdl-access=free }}</ref>

